rization","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:5ce0c3ae76cadc1520258e2bd8dbaed8de5a2f3310f4f8dfb28ded48ebb4f494","file":"preprints/Finite-Congruence-Lattices-Characterization-and-Undecidability-September-24-2026/build/sections/graph.tex","line":33,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"49c34b14f5e204609c4266e51980a9c0ba781241d232a50f071783bce0d122b9","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Finite-Congruence-Lattices-Characterization-and-Undecidability-September-24-2026/build/sections/graph.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:5ce0c3ae76cadc1520258e2bd8dbaed8de5a2f3310f4f8dfb28ded48ebb4f494","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Finite-Congruence-Lattices-Characterization-and-Undecidability-September-24-2026/build/sections/graph.tex#L33"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{f:criterion}\nThe lattice $L$ is the full congruence lattice of a finite algebra if and only\nif there is an $L$-colored complete graph $(A,d)$ satisfying all three\nconditions below.\n\\begin{enumerate}[label=\\textup{(\\roman*)}]\n\\item\\label{f:graph-triangle} If $p\\ne q$, then $d(p,q)\\ne0$, and\n\\[\n d(p,q)\\le d(p,u)\\vee d(u,q)\\qquad(p,q,u\\in A).\n\\]\n\\item\\label{f:graph-reflection} Whenever $a\\not\\le b$ in $L$, there are vertices\n$p,q$ with $d(p,q)\\le a$ and $d(p,q)\\not\\le b$.\n\\item\\label{f:graph-connectivity} For every nonempty edge set $S$, vertices\n$p,q$ satisfying $d(p,q)\\le a_S$ lie in the same connected component of\n$\\Gamma_S$.\n\\end{enumerate}\nFor each fixed $|A|$, these conditions involve only lattice inequalities,\nfinite vertex labelings, and paths."}
